    "detailed_description": "<strong>Gameplay:</strong><br>- Black Beacon Hill is a top-down bullet hell shooter with a unique and extremely minimalistic core mechanic: All player attacks, movements, and actions are pre-scripted automatically launched. Players only control the aim of these actions. Which means:<br>- <strong>There are zero buttons to press, and no controls besides mouse movement.</strong> <br>And it looks like this:<br><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2641070/extras/717687268ef9edcffcf84c8fee9ba37a.poster.avif?t=1719947776\" width=480 height=270 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2641070/extras/717687268ef9edcffcf84c8fee9ba37a.webm?t=1719947776\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2641070/extras/717687268ef9edcffcf84c8fee9ba37a.mp4?t=1719947776\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></span><br>- Each stage contains it's own piece of original soundtrack. Composed by Chris Jay. <br><br><strong>Story:</strong><br><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2641070/extras/cf12230fe0419f383770fca95cfe5d13.avif?t=1719947776\" width=500 height=282 /></span><br>- <u>[The high chamber]</u> finds itself in a precarious position. Domestically, challengers against it's iron grip over Ulstania had begin to rear their heads from the senate and the civil police force. Beyond its borders, the long war it instigated against Kostakovia had become an unwinnable slugfest yielding only scortched earth at the cost of countless Ulstanian lives. Meanwhile, the sudden loss of communication with the front and whispers of a rogue cyberweapon herald a greater crisis on the horizon...<br>- Caught in the middle are the <u>[Phantoms]</u> - Hired operators of the high chamber. The few surviving veterans of the war with nowhere else to go. Making a living off doing the dirty work of their employers. Trying to ignore the open secret that, one way or another, this arrangement will not last...<br><br>- An originally written visual novel that plays out in between and within each stage.<br><br><br><strong>Future Arcs:</strong><br>- TBA",
